{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>On account of his son</b> — that he would turn out for a bad upbringing. But its simple sense is: on account of her saying to him to send him away. This is the language of Rashi (Rashi on Genesis 21:11). And what seems correct in my eyes is that Scripture tells of Abraham's honor, and says that the matter was not very evil in his eyes because of desire for his concubine and his wish for her — had she told him only to send the maidservant away, he would have done Sarah's will. But on account of his son it was very grievous to him, and he did not want to listen to her. And HaShem said to him: let it not be evil in his eyes on account of the lad or on account of the maidservant at all, and let him listen to Sarah's voice, for in Isaac alone shall his name be called to him, and Ishmael shall not be called his seed. And because Abraham feared for him, lest harm befall him when he sent him away from himself, He said that He would make him into a nation and bless him, because he is truly his seed."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:33:14.296987028Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}